# SWHP Frontend Implementation Tasks

This task list serves as the actionable checklist for building the SWHP React frontend, derived from the technical design plan.

## 1. Environment & Routing Setup
- [ ] Initialize the React application (e.g., using Vite `npm create vite@latest swhp-frontend`).
- [ ] Install required core dependencies (`react-router-dom`, `axios`, `bootstrap`, `fortawesome`).
- [ ] Setup global routing configuration (`/login`, `/register`, `/profile`, `/apply`, `/payment`, `/dashboard`).
- [ ] Configure `axios` interceptors to handle JWT injection and centralized error handling (e.g., redirect on 401).

## 2. Authentication & Identity
- [ ] Create Context API (`AuthContext`) for global session management.
- [ ] Build the `Login` and `Register` UI components.
- [ ] Implement legacy account mapping UI (`AccountMapping`) to capture credentials for mapping to SWHP.
- [ ] Implement Password Recovery components (`ForgotPassword` and `ResetPassword`).

## 3. Profile & Service Selection
- [ ] Develop the `UserProfile` component for collecting common cross-system fields.
- [ ] Build the `ServiceSelection` dashboard, rendering available legacy services (NHS, FDA, etc.).
- [ ] Implement logic to submit selected services to `/api/v1/swan/create` and store the generated SWAN.

## 4. iFrame Orchestration
- [ ] Create the `ServiceIframe` wrapper component for loading individual legacy forms.
- [ ] Implement state management for the service queue (advancing forms sequentially).
- [ ] Add the `window.addEventListener('message')` listener on the parent.
- [ ] Implement strict `event.origin` validation and verify the `eventType === 'FormCompleted'` and `payload.swan` match.

## 5. Consolidated Payment & Tracking
- [ ] Build the `PaymentSummary` component to fetch and display the aggregated fee breakdown from `/api/v1/swan/{swan}/fees`.
- [ ] Integrate the "Initiate Payment" redirect logic.
- [ ] Develop the `ApplicationTracking` dashboard to fetch and list real-time status of submitted applications.

## 6. Security & Finalization
- [ ] Integrate CAPTCHA into public auth views.
- [ ] Ensure all forms use strict validation and handle API errors gracefully.
- [ ] Verify CSRF defenses and ensure no sensitive data is placed in localStorage.
